class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int left = 0, right = nums.size() - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;
            else if (nums[mid] < target)
                left = mid + 1;
            else
                right = mid - 1;
        }

        return left;
    }
};

**Intuition:**  
The array is sorted, so binary search can find the target efficiently.  
If the target is absent, `left` gives its correct insertion position.

**Algorithm:**  
Compare the target with the middle element and eliminate half of the search space.  
Continue until the search ends, then return `left`.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(log n)**  
Space: **O(1)**
